title: Wildcat Strikes!
subtitle: Strikes have begun, against the wishes of union leaders.
view-if: burgfrieden = 1
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
	Q.union_strength -= 3
	Q.union_unrest += 3

	Q.workers_spd += 4*(1-Q.dissent)
!}
tags: event

= Wildcat Strikes!

Workers in unions have defied their leaders, and have gone on strike in several industries.

Workers in several industries have gone on strike, in defiance of their leaders and of the Burgfrieden political truce.

It is up to us to support these strikes, or order them back to work.

- @return_work: Ask they return to work.
- @support: Aid the striking workers.
- @nothing: Let the strikes handle themselves.

@return_work
subtitle: +1 resources
on-arrival: {!
	Q.resources += 1

	Q.union_unrest += 5
	Q.union_support -= 5
	Q.grassroots_support -= 4

	Q.new_middle_spd += 2
	Q.old_middle_spd += 3
	Q.workers_spd -= 4
	Q.unemployed_spd -= 3
!}

The workers are unhappy with this. The middle class views the SPD in a more positive light however. Some have even donated.

@support
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
	Q.resources -= 1

	Q.union_strength += 3
	Q.union_support += 4

	Q.workers_spd += 5*(1-Q.dissent)
!}

This is unpopular amongst the right wing of the party. They view this as destabilizing and disrupting the war effort.

@nothing
on-arrival: {!
	Q.union_support -= 3
	Q.union_unrest += 3

	Q.workers_spd -= 3
	Q.grassroots_support -= 4
!}

